    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/6/96624.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 251,
    "turn_text": "Well, some of them are paid to do it. Right. Some of them are motivated by these carbon polluters who make tons of money from it. First of all, the coal industry is dying for sure. And we got to take care of the coal miners. Most of their jobs were eliminated by the coal companies with automation a long time ago. But, and by the way, the famous coal museum in Kentucky, in the heart of coal country, just switched to solar electricity. That's in the movie, right? But they're saving money. But I think one of the reasons why- That's",
