  {
    "episode_id": 96624,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/6/96624.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 254,
    "turn_text": "I think one of the reasons why Trump made the coal thing a big deal was that he benefited from some widespread anger on the part of people who have watched middle-class wages stagnate for decades, and they're angry about the current pattern of globalization and outsourcing, and now intelligent automation is coming in and making some of that. The job loss is even worse. But that's not a partisan",
