    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/6/96624.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 305,
    "turn_text": "There was a book that came out a few years ago called The Innovator's Dilemma. of making the same point that if you got a business and it's based on a particular plan and somebody comes to you with a brand new idea for something that's cheaper and better and you're looking at it and you say wow I could invest in this and then you pause and say But if I do, then it's gonna destroy this business I've got going and I've sunk all my assets into this legacy business and I'm never gonna make as much money with this new better approach. And so what some of them do is decide to just hang on and try to fool people and obscure the truth about it and keep making as much money for as long as they can from the old ways.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_00",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
