    "turn_idx": 319,
    "turn_text": "to learn from a great professor from here in California. Guy's name was Roger Ravel. He was the first scientist to measure CO2 in the atmosphere. And he's the one who opened my eyes to this. Some seven, eight years after that, when I was elected to Congress, I asked what's going on with global warming and nothing was. So I helped organize the first hearing on it. And I invited my professor to come and be the lead-off witness. And I thought it would have a big impact down there, but it didn't. And that's when I first started asking myself, how can this be communicated more effectively so that I can recreate for others the aha moment that I had learning from this professor and it's been a lifelong journey since then.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_00",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
